silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_03_cite_as_kleisli_arrow_yoneda_hom_leg_3 silm:hasExample "In 'CiteKleisliLegGlueKl', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §20.1 plus JoC §11.3: glue^Kl: TypedLeg_record -> Free(Sigma)(Apex) commits the typed record leg to the colimit cocone D_Mittens via lambda_rec. For the Mittens fixture the record leg is VetRecord77 typed via the record sort; glue is the cocone-assembly step that confirms the cite-unit was correctly placed in the four-arrow chain ending at Mittens." .
